# Note: to make our life easier, we now sync every change from the upstream
# maintainance branch (release/${VER}/master) into AOSC-Tracking with the
# UPSTREAM: tag when we update core minor version or patch level.  Assuming
# the remote referring to the upstream repo is "origin" and the one
# referring to AOSC-Tracking is "aosc" in your glibc git repo, it can be
# done via:
#
# git fetch origin
# git fetch aosc
# git branch -D aosc/glibc-${VER}
# git checkout aosc/glibc-${VER}
# GIT_SEQUENCE_EDITOR=vim                    \
# GIT_EDITOR="sed -i -e '1s/^/UPSTREAM: /'"  \
# git rebase glibc-${VER}
#
# On another terminal, change into the glibc repo and issue
#
# LAST_FROM=21442dba0d0b
# LAST_TO=cb648f28f165
# git log ${LAST_PICK}..origin/release/2.44/master --pretty='r %h' --reverse
#
# and paste the output into the vim window, after the line picking commit
# ${LAST_TO}.  Then if you need any commits from the master branch or the
# list,  put a "break" line after those pasted lines and apply them during
# the break.
#
# You may need to skip some empty commits in case a patch previously picked
# from master or list as they are likely applied in the release branch
# already.
#
# Once the branch looks correct, push it to AOSC-Tracking and update
# LAST_FROM and LAST_TO above.
#
# Finally rebase aosc/${VER}-ow branch onto aosc/${VER} for
# runtime-emulation/liblol.
